    <!-- EDITORIAL & METHODOLOGICAL KNOWLEDGE SECTION (E-E-A-T) -->
    <article style="border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0; padding-top: 3.5rem; line-height: 1.85; color: #334155;">
      
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.85rem; font-weight: 800; color: #0f172a; margin-bottom: 1rem; letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
        Theoretical Principles of Liquid-Phase Adsorption Isotherms
      </h2>
      <p>
        Adsorption isotherm modeling describes the fractional distribution of mobile sorbate molecules between an aqueous phase and solid porous matrices at equilibrium. Establishing accurate mathematical fits is critical for sizing batch reactors, estimating monolayer coverage on metal-organic frameworks (MOFs) and functionalized silicas, and designing municipal wastewater decontamination units.
      </p>

      <h3 style="font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 800; color: #0f172a; margin-top: 2rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
        1. The Langmuir Isotherm &amp; The Separation Factor (R<sub>L</sub>)
      </h3>
      <p>
        Formulated by Irving Langmuir in 1918, the model posits that adsorption occurs on energetically uniform, identical localized sites with zero lateral interaction between adjacent adsorbed species. Once a molecule occupies a site, no further sorption can take place at that locus:
      </p>
      <div style="background: #f8fafc; border-left: 4px solid #0284c7; padding: 1rem; margin: 1.25rem 0; font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: 0.95rem;">
        Non-Linear: qe = (qmax * KL * Ce) / (1 + KL * Ce)<br />
        Linear (Type 1): Ce / qe = (1 / (qmax * KL)) + (Ce / qmax)
      </div>
      <p>
        The essential feasibility of the Langmuir system is expressed via the dimensionless equilibrium parameter or separation factor (R<sub>L</sub>):
      </p>
      <div style="background: #f8fafc; border-left: 4px solid #0284c7; padding: 1rem; margin: 1.25rem 0; font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: 0.95rem;">
        RL = 1 / (1 + KL * C0)
      </div>
      <p>
        Where C<sub>0</sub> is the initial concentration. The value of R<sub>L</sub> indicates the shape of the isotherm:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>R<sub>L</sub> &gt; 1:</strong> Unfavorable adsorption kinetics.</li>
        <li><strong>R<sub>L</sub> = 1:</strong> Linear adsorption (no preferential affinity).</li>
        <li><strong>0 &lt; R<sub>L</sub> &lt; 1:</strong> Favorable adsorption mechanism.</li>
        <li><strong>R<sub>L</sub> = 0:</strong> Irreversible chemical fixation.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 style="font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 800; color: #0f172a; margin-top: 2rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
        2. The Freundlich Isotherm (Surface Heterogeneity)
      </h3>
      <p>
        The Freundlich equation is an empirical formulation that accounts for non-ideal, reversible sorption across heterogeneous surfaces with an exponential energy distribution:
      </p>
      <div style="background: #f8fafc; border-left: 4px solid #0284c7; padding: 1rem; margin: 1.25rem 0; font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: 0.95rem;">
        Non-Linear: qe = KF * (Ce)^(1/n)<br />
        Linear: ln(qe) = ln(KF) + (1/n) * ln(Ce)
      </div>
      <p>
        Here, K<sub>F</sub> denotes the relative sorption capacity, while 1/n is the heterogeneity factor. When 1/n &lt; 1, adsorption is normal and favorable; values of n between 2 and 10 represent excellent adsorption intensity.
      </p>

      <h3 style="font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 800; color: #0f172a; margin-top: 2rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
        3. Dubinin-Radushkevich Model &amp; Mean Free Energy (E)
      </h3>
      <p>
        The Dubinin-Radushkevich (D-R) isotherm does not assume a homogeneous surface or constant sorption potential. By applying the Polanyi potential (&epsilon; = R T ln(1 + 1/C<sub>e</sub>)), it extracts the mean free energy of adsorption per molecule (E), diagnosing the fundamental sorption mechanism:
      </p>
      <div style="background: #f8fafc; border-left: 4px solid #0284c7; padding: 1rem; margin: 1.25rem 0; font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: 0.95rem;">
        E = 1 / sqrt(2 * beta) [kJ/mol]
      </div>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>E &lt; 8 kJ/mol:</strong> Physical adsorption governed by van der Waals dispersion forces.</li>
        <li><strong>8 &le; E &le; 16 kJ/mol:</strong> Ion-exchange or electrostatic coordination.</li>
        <li><strong>E &gt; 16 kJ/mol:</strong> Chemical adsorption (chemisorption) with covalent/coordinate bonding.</li>
      </ul>

      <!-- FAQs Accordion -->
      <h3 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 800; color: #0f172a; margin-top: 3rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
        Frequently Asked Questions: Adsorption Equilibrium Analysis
      </h3>

      <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.85rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <details style="background: #ffffff; border: 1.5px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.15rem;">
          <summary style="font-weight: 800; color: #0f172a; cursor: pointer; font-size: 0.95rem;">Why do linear regression transforms introduce mathematical error?</summary>
          <p style="margin: 0.65rem 0 0 0; font-size: 0.9rem; color: #334155; line-height: 1.7;">
            Linear transformations alter the error variance structure of experimental data. For example, in the Type 1 Langmuir plot (C<sub>e</sub>/q<sub>e</sub> vs C<sub>e</sub>), low concentration points with small q<sub>e</sub> receive disproportionate weight. Comparing non-linear metrics such as Root Mean Square Error (RMSE) and Reduced Chi-Square (&chi;<sup>2</sup>) alongside R<sup>2</sup> prevents erroneous conclusions.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details style="background: #ffffff; border: 1.5px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.15rem;">
          <summary style="font-weight: 800; color: #0f172a; cursor: pointer; font-size: 0.95rem;">How many experimental points are required for a publishable isotherm?</summary>
          <p style="margin: 0.65rem 0 0 0; font-size: 0.9rem; color: #334155; line-height: 1.7;">
            Peer-reviewed journals typically expect a minimum of 5 to 8 distinct equilibrium concentrations spanning from low sub-saturation levels up to the plateau region where adsorbent sites approach saturation.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>

    </article>

  </main>

  <script>
    import { 
      parseCleanNumber,
      convertVolumeToLiters,
      convertMassToGrams,
      calculateBatchQe,
      solveAdsorptionTournament,
      type IsothermPoint
    } from '../utils/isothermMath';

    // Benchmark Presets
    const PRESETS: Record<string, Array<{ c0: number; ce: number; v: number; m: number; qe: number }>> = {
      mb: [
        { c0: 25, ce: 1.2, v: 0.1, m: 0.05, qe: 47.6 },
        { c0: 50, ce: 4.8, v: 0.1, m: 0.05, qe: 90.4 },
        { c0: 100, ce: 14.5, v: 0.1, m: 0.05, qe: 171.0 },
        { c0: 150, ce: 32.0, v: 0.1, m: 0.05, qe: 236.0 },
        { c0: 200, ce: 58.2, v: 0.1, m: 0.05, qe: 283.6 },
        { c0: 250, ce: 94.0, v: 0.1, m: 0.05, qe: 312.0 }
      ],
      paraquat: [
        { c0: 10, ce: 0.8, v: 0.05, m: 0.02, qe: 23.0 },
        { c0: 25, ce: 3.2, v: 0.05, m: 0.02, qe: 54.5 },
        { c0: 50, ce: 9.5, v: 0.05, m: 0.02, qe: 101.25 },
        { c0: 75, ce: 18.0, v: 0.05, m: 0.02, qe: 142.5 },
        { c0: 100, ce: 31.0, v: 0.05, m: 0.02, qe: 172.5 },
        { c0: 150, ce: 64.0, v: 0.05, m: 0.02, qe: 215.0 }
      ],
      lead: [
        { c0: 20, ce: 0.5, v: 0.05, m: 0.025, qe: 39.0 },
        { c0: 50, ce: 2.1, v: 0.05, m: 0.025, qe: 95.8 },
        { c0: 100, ce: 8.4, v: 0.05, m: 0.025, qe: 183.2 },
        { c0: 200, ce: 28.0, v: 0.05, m: 0.025, qe: 344.0 },
        { c0: 300, ce: 62.0, v: 0.05, m: 0.025, qe: 476.0 },
        { c0: 400, ce: 115.0, v: 0.05, m: 0.025, qe: 570.0 }
      ]
    };

    // State Variables
    let isBatchMode = true;
    let dataPoints: IsothermPoint[] = [];

    // DOM Elements
    const btnModeBatch = document.getElementById('btnModeBatch')!;
    const btnModeDirect = document.getElementById('btnModeDirect')!;
    const batchVolMassSelectors = document.getElementById('batchVolMassSelectors')!;
    const isothermTableBody = document.getElementById('isothermTableBody')!;
    const btnAddRowBtn = document.getElementById('btnAddRowBtn')!;
    const btnClearTableBtn = document.getElementById('btnClearTableBtn')!;
    const fileUploadInput = document.getElementById('fileUploadInput') as HTMLInputElement;
    const inpTempK = document.getElementById('inpTempK') as HTMLInputElement;
    const selVolUnit = document.getElementById('selVolUnit') as HTMLSelectElement;
    const selMassUnit = document.getElementById('selMassUnit') as HTMLSelectElement;

    function initializeData() {
      const saved = localStorage.getItem('cd_isotherm_points');
      if (saved) {
        try {
          dataPoints = JSON.parse(saved);
        } catch {
          loadPreset('mb');
        }
      } else {
        loadPreset('mb');
      }
    }

    function loadPreset(key: string) {
      const items = PRESETS[key] || PRESETS.mb;
      dataPoints = items.map((p, idx) => ({
        id: 'pt_' + Date.now() + '_' + idx,
        c0: p.c0,
        ce: p.ce,
        v: p.v,
        m: p.m,
        qe: p.qe
      }));
      renderTable();
      recalculate();
    }

    // Toggle Modes
    btnModeBatch.addEventListener('click', () => {
      isBatchMode = true;
      btnModeBatch.style.background = '#0284c7';
      btnModeBatch.style.color = '#ffffff';
      btnModeDirect.style.background = 'transparent';
      btnModeDirect.style.color = '#64748b';
      batchVolMassSelectors.style.display = 'flex';
      document.getElementById('thC0')!.style.display = '';
      document.getElementById('thVol')!.style.display = '';
      document.getElementById('thMass')!.style.display = '';
      renderTable();
      recalculate();
    });

    btnModeDirect.addEventListener('click', () => {
      isBatchMode = false;
      btnModeDirect.style.background = '#0284c7';
      btnModeDirect.style.color = '#ffffff';
      btnModeBatch.style.background = 'transparent';
      btnModeBatch.style.color = '#64748b';
      batchVolMassSelectors.style.display = 'none';
      document.getElementById('thC0')!.style.display = 'none';
      document.getElementById('thVol')!.style.display = 'none';
      document.getElementById('thMass')!.style.display = 'none';
      renderTable();
      recalculate();
    });

    // Preset button events
    document.querySelectorAll('.preset-btn').forEach(btn => {
      btn.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
        const pKey = (e.currentTarget as HTMLElement).dataset.preset || 'mb';
        loadPreset(pKey);
      });
    });

    // Render Table Rows
    function renderTable() {
      isothermTableBody.innerHTML = '';
      dataPoints.forEach((p, idx) => {
        const tr = document.createElement('tr');
        tr.style.borderBottom = '1px solid #f1f5f9';

        if (isBatchMode) {
          tr.innerHTML = `
            <td style="padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem; text-align: center; color: #94a3b8; font-weight: bold;">${idx + 1}</td>
            <td style="padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem;"><input type="text" inputmode="decimal" class="grid-input" data-idx="${idx}" data-field="c0" value="${p.c0 ?? ''}" style="width: 85px; padding: 0.35rem 0.5rem; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: bold;" /></td>
            <td style="padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem;"><input type="text" inputmode="decimal" class="grid-input" data-idx="${idx}" data-field="ce" value="${p.ce ?? ''}" style="width: 85px; padding: 0.35rem 0.5rem; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: bold;" /></td>
            <td style="padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem;"><input type="text" inputmode="decimal" class="grid-input" data-idx="${idx}" data-field="v" value="${p.v ?? 0.1}" style="width: 75px; padding: 0.35rem 0.5rem; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.85rem;" /></td>
            <td style="padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem;"><input type="text" inputmode="decimal" class="grid-input" data-idx="${idx}" data-field="m" value="${p.m ?? 0.05}" style="width: 75px; padding: 0.35rem 0.5rem; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.85rem;" /></td>
            <td style="padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem; font-weight: 800; color: #0284c7; background: #f0f9ff; font-family: monospace;">${p.qe.toFixed(2)}</td>
            <td style="padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem; text-align: center;"><button type="button" class="del-row-btn" data-idx="${idx}" style="background: none; border: none; cursor: pointer; color: #ef4444; font-weight: bold;">✕</button></td>
          `;
        } else {
          tr.innerHTML = `
            <td style="padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem; text-align: center; color: #94a3b8; font-weight: bold;">${idx + 1}</td>
            <td style="padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem;"><input type="text" inputmode="decimal" class="grid-input" data-idx="${idx}" data-field="ce" value="${p.ce ?? ''}" style="width: 100px; padding: 0.35rem 0.5rem; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: bold;" /></td>
            <td style="padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem;"><input type="text" inputmode="decimal" class="grid-input" data-idx="${idx}" data-field="qe" value="${p.qe ?? ''}" style="width: 100px; padding: 0.35rem 0.5rem; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: bold; color: #0284c7;" /></td>
            <td style="padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem; text-align: center;"><button type="button" class="del-row-btn" data-idx="${idx}" style="background: none; border: none; cursor: pointer; color: #ef4444; font-weight: bold;">✕</button></td>
          `;
        }
        isothermTableBody.appendChild(tr);
      });

      // Attach row change events
      document.querySelectorAll('.grid-input').forEach(inp => {
        inp.addEventListener('input', handleCellEdit);
      });

      document.querySelectorAll('.del-row-btn').forEach(btn => {
        btn.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
          const idx = parseInt((e.currentTarget as HTMLElement).dataset.idx || '0', 10);
          dataPoints.splice(idx, 1);
          renderTable();
          recalculate();
        });
      });
    }

    function handleCellEdit(e: Event) {
      const target = e.currentTarget as HTMLInputElement;
      const idx = parseInt(target.dataset.idx || '0', 10);
      const field = target.dataset.field || 'ce';
      const val = parseCleanNumber(target.value);

      if (!dataPoints[idx]) return;

      if (field === 'c0') dataPoints[idx].c0 = val;
      if (field === 'ce') dataPoints[idx].ce = val;
      if (field === 'v') dataPoints[idx].v = val;
      if (field === 'm') dataPoints[idx].m = val;
      if (field === 'qe') dataPoints[idx].qe = val;

      if (isBatchMode) {
        const vLit = convertVolumeToLiters(dataPoints[idx].v || 0.1, selVolUnit.value as any);
        const mG = convertMassToGrams(dataPoints[idx].m || 0.05, selMassUnit.value as any);
        dataPoints[idx].qe = calculateBatchQe(dataPoints[idx].c0 || 0, dataPoints[idx].ce || 0, vLit, mG);
      }

      saveData();
      renderTableValuesOnly();
      recalculate();
    }

    function renderTableValuesOnly() {
      const rows = isothermTableBody.querySelectorAll('tr');
      dataPoints.forEach((p, idx) => {
        if (rows[idx]) {
          const qeCell = rows[idx].querySelector('td:nth-last-child(2)');
          if (qeCell && isBatchMode) {
            qeCell.textContent = p.qe.toFixed(2);
          }
        }
      });
    }

    function addRow() {
      const last = dataPoints[dataPoints.length - 1] || { c0: 50, ce: 10, v: 0.1, m: 0.05, qe: 80 };
      dataPoints.push({
        id: 'pt_' + Date.now(),
        c0: (last.c0 || 50) + 25,
        ce: (last.ce || 10) + 15,
        v: last.v || 0.1,
        m: last.m || 0.05,
        qe: (last.qe || 80) + 40
      });
      renderTable();
      recalculate();
    }

    btnAddRowBtn.addEventListener('click', addRow);

    btnClearTableBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      dataPoints = [];
      renderTable();
      recalculate();
    });

    // File Upload
    fileUploadInput.addEventListener('change', (e) => {
      const file = (e.target as HTMLInputElement).files?.[0];
      if (!file) return;

      const reader = new FileReader();
      reader.onload = (evt) => {
        const text = evt.target?.result as string;
        if (!text) return;

        const lines = text.split(/\r?\n/).filter(l => l.trim().length > 0);
        const newPts: IsothermPoint[] = [];

        lines.forEach((line, idx) => {
          if (idx === 0 && (line.toLowerCase().includes('c') || line.toLowerCase().includes('q'))) return;
          const parts = line.split(/[,\t;]+/).map(p => parseCleanNumber(p.trim()));
          if (parts.length >= 2) {
            if (parts.length >= 4) {
              const c0 = parts[0], ce = parts[1], v = parts[2], m = parts[3];
              newPts.push({ id: 'csv_' + idx, c0, ce, v, m, qe: calculateBatchQe(c0, ce, v, m) });
            } else {
              newPts.push({ id: 'csv_' + idx, ce: parts[0], qe: parts[1] });
            }
          }
        });

        if (newPts.length > 0) {
          dataPoints = newPts;
          renderTable();
          recalculate();
        }
      };
      reader.readAsText(file);
    });

    function saveData() {
      localStorage.setItem('cd_isotherm_points', JSON.stringify(dataPoints));
    }

    // Recalculate & Multi-Model Tournament
    let lastTournamentResult: any = null;

    function recalculate() {
      const tempK = parseCleanNumber(inpTempK.value) || 298.15;
      const validPoints = dataPoints.filter(p => p.ce > 0 && p.qe > 0);

      if (validPoints.length < 2) {
        document.getElementById('bestModelTitle')!.textContent = 'Awaiting Data';
        document.getElementById('bestModelR2Badge')!.textContent = 'R² = --';
        document.getElementById('mechanismVerdictText')!.textContent = 'Enter at least 2 non-zero data points.';
        document.getElementById('tournamentTableBody')!.innerHTML = '';
        document.getElementById('extractedParamsGrid')!.innerHTML = '';
        clearSvg();
        return;
      }

      const res = solveAdsorptionTournament(validPoints, tempK);
      lastTournamentResult = res;

      // Update Best Model Header
      document.getElementById('bestModelTitle')!.textContent = res.bestModel + ' Model';
      document.getElementById('bestModelR2Badge')!.textContent = `R² = ${res.bestR2.toFixed(4)}`;
      document.getElementById('mechanismVerdictText')!.textContent = res.adsorptionMechanism;

      // Render Tournament Table
      const tBody = document.getElementById('tournamentTableBody')!;
      tBody.innerHTML = '';
      const models = [res.langmuir, res.freundlich, res.temkin, res.dubininRadushkevich];

      models.forEach(m => {
        const isBest = m.modelName === res.bestModel;
        const tr = document.createElement('tr');
        tr.style.borderBottom = '1px solid #f1f5f9';
        if (isBest) tr.style.background = '#f0f9ff';
        tr.innerHTML = `
          <td style="padding: 0.45rem 0.65rem; font-weight: ${isBest ? '800' : '600'}; color: ${isBest ? '#0284c7' : '#1e293b'};">
            ${m.modelName} ${isBest ? '🏆' : ''}
          </td>
          <td style="padding: 0.45rem 0.65rem; text-align: right; font-weight: bold; font-family: monospace;">${m.r2.toFixed(4)}</td>
          <td style="padding: 0.45rem 0.65rem; text-align: right; font-family: monospace;">${m.rmse.toFixed(3)}</td>
          <td style="padding: 0.45rem 0.65rem; text-align: right; font-family: monospace;">${m.chiSquare.toFixed(3)}</td>
        `;
        tBody.appendChild(tr);
      });

      // Render Key Extracted Parameters
      const pGrid = document.getElementById('extractedParamsGrid')!;
      pGrid.innerHTML = '';
      const pL = res.langmuir.parameters;
      const pF = res.freundlich.parameters;
      const pD = res.dubininRadushkevich.parameters;

      const cards = [
        { label: 'Langmuir qmax', val: `${pL.qmax?.value.toFixed(2) ?? '--'} mg/g` },
        { label: 'Affinity (KL)', val: `${pL.kL?.value.toFixed(4) ?? '--'} L/mg` },
        { label: 'Freundlich KF', val: `${pF.kF?.value.toFixed(2) ?? '--'}` },
        { label: 'Heterogeneity (1/n)', val: `${pF.invN?.value.toFixed(3) ?? '--'}` },
        { label: 'D-R Energy (E)', val: `${pD.E?.value.toFixed(2) ?? '--'} kJ/mol` },
        { label: 'Mean Feasibility (RL)', val: res.rlCurve[0] ? `${res.rlCurve[0].rl.toFixed(3)} (${res.rlCurve[0].status})` : '--' }
      ];

      cards.forEach(c => {
        const div = document.createElement('div');
        div.style.cssText = 'background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 6px; padding: 0.5rem;';
        div.innerHTML = `
          <div style="font-size: 0.7rem; color: #64748b; font-weight: 700;">${c.label}</div>
          <div style="font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 800; color: #0f172a; margin-top: 2px;">${c.val}</div>
        `;
        pGrid.appendChild(div);
      });

      // Render SVG Chart
      renderSvgChart(validPoints, res);
    }

    // Dynamic SVG Chart Engine
    function renderSvgChart(points: IsothermPoint[], res: any) {
      const svg = document.getElementById('isothermSvg')!;
      const w = 500;
      const h = 320;
      const padL = 55;
      const padR = 25;
      const padT = 25;
      const padB = 40;

      const maxCe = Math.max(...points.map(p => p.ce)) * 1.15 || 10;
      const maxQe = Math.max(...points.map(p => p.qe)) * 1.2 || 10;

      const scaleX = (val: number) => padL + (val / maxCe) * (w - padL - padR);
      const scaleY = (val: number) => h - padB - (val / maxQe) * (h - padT - padB);

      let svgHtml = `
        <line x1="${padL}" y1="${h - padB}" x2="${w - padR}" y2="${h - padB}" stroke="#cbd5e1" stroke-width="2"/>
        <line x1="${padL}" y1="${padT}" x2="${padL}" y2="${h - padB}" stroke="#cbd5e1" stroke-width="2"/>
        <text x="${w / 2}" y="${h - 8}" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="#475569" font-weight="bold">Equilibrium Concentration Ce (${(document.getElementById('selConcUnit') as HTMLSelectElement).value})</text>
        <text x="14" y="${h / 2}" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="#475569" font-weight="bold" transform="rotate(-90 14 ${h / 2})">Adsorption Uptake qe (mg/g)</text>
      `;

      // Draw Grid Ticks
      for (let i = 0; i <= 4; i++) {
        const xVal = (maxCe / 4) * i;
        const yVal = (maxQe / 4) * i;
        const xPos = scaleX(xVal);
        const yPos = scaleY(yVal);

        svgHtml += `
          <text x="${xPos}" y="${h - padB + 14}" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9" fill="#94a3b8">${xVal.toFixed(0)}</text>
          <text x="${padL - 6}" y="${yPos + 3}" text-anchor="end" font-size="9" fill="#94a3b8">${yVal.toFixed(0)}</text>
          <line x1="${padL}" y1="${yPos}" x2="${w - padR}" y2="${yPos}" stroke="#f1f5f9" stroke-width="1"/>
        `;
      }

      // Draw Langmuir Curve
      let langD = '';
      for (let cx = 0; cx <= maxCe; cx += maxCe / 40) {
        const qPred = res.langmuir.predictQe(cx);
        const px = scaleX(cx);
        const py = scaleY(qPred);
        langD += (cx === 0 ? `M ${px} ${py}` : ` L ${px} ${py}`);
      }
      svgHtml += `<path d="${langD}" fill="none" stroke="#0284c7" stroke-width="2.5" />`;

      // Draw Freundlich Curve
      let freundD = '';
      for (let cx = maxCe / 40; cx <= maxCe; cx += maxCe / 40) {
        const qPred = res.freundlich.predictQe(cx);
        const px = scaleX(cx);
        const py = scaleY(qPred);
        freundD += (freundD === '' ? `M ${px} ${py}` : ` L ${px} ${py}`);
      }
      svgHtml += `<path d="${freundD}" fill="none" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="4,3" />`;

      // Draw Experimental Points
      points.forEach(p => {
        const cx = scaleX(p.ce);
        const cy = scaleY(p.qe);
        svgHtml += `
          <circle cx="${cx}" cy="${cy}" r="4.5" fill="#0f172a" stroke="#ffffff" stroke-width="1.5"/>
        `;
      });

      svg.innerHTML = svgHtml;
    }

    function clearSvg() {
      const svg = document.getElementById('isothermSvg')!;
      svg.innerHTML = '<text x="250" y="160" text-anchor="middle" fill="#94a3b8" font-size="12">Enter at least 2 points to generate isotherm curve</text>';
    }

    // CSV Export
    document.getElementById('btnExportCsv')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (!dataPoints.length) return;
      let csv = 'Initial_C0,Equilibrium_Ce,Volume_L,Mass_g,Uptake_qe_mg_g\n';
      dataPoints.forEach(p => {
        csv += `${p.c0 ?? ''},${p.ce},${p.v ?? ''},${p.m ?? ''},${p.qe.toFixed(4)}\n`;
      });
      const blob = new Blob([csv], { type: 'text/csv' });
      const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
      const a = document.createElement('a');
      a.href = url;
      a.download = `isotherm_data_${Date.now()}.csv`;
      a.click();
    });

    // Copy Overleaf / LaTeX Equation Block
    document.getElementById('btnCopyLatex')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (!lastTournamentResult) return;
      const qmax = lastTournamentResult.langmuir.parameters.qmax?.value.toFixed(2);
      const kL = lastTournamentResult.langmuir.parameters.kL?.value.toFixed(4);
      const r2L = lastTournamentResult.langmuir.r2.toFixed(4);

      const latex = `% Adsorption Isotherm Fitted Parameters (ChemistryDesk)
\\begin{equation}
  q_e = \\frac{q_{\\max} K_L C_e}{1 + K_L C_e} = \\frac{${qmax} \\times ${kL} \\times C_e}{1 + ${kL} C_e} \\quad (R^2 = ${r2L})
\\end{equation}`;
      navigator.clipboard.writeText(latex);
      alert('LaTeX equation block copied to clipboard for Overleaf.');
    });

    // Academic Citation System
    const citeDrawer = document.getElementById('citeDrawer');
    const toggleCiteBtn = document.getElementById('toggleCiteBtn');
    const inlineCiteOutput = document.getElementById('inlineCiteOutput');
    const inlineTabs = document.querySelectorAll('.inline-cite-tab');
    const inlineCopyBtn = document.getElementById('inlineCopyCiteBtn');

    const doi = "10.5281/zenodo.23059466";
    const currentYear = new Date().getFullYear();

    const citations: Record<string, string> = {
      bibtex: `@software{khan_chemistrydesk_isotherm_${currentYear},
  author       = {Khan, Bilal},
  title        = {ChemistryDesk: Adsorption Isotherm Studio (Langmuir, Freundlich, Temkin, D-R)},
  year         = {${currentYear}},
  version      = {v1.0.1},
  publisher    = {Zenodo},
  doi          = {${doi}},
  url          = {https://chemistrydesk.vercel.app/isotherm}
}`,
      acs: `Khan, B. ChemistryDesk: Adsorption Isotherm Studio, version 1.0.1; Zenodo, ${currentYear}. https://doi.org/${doi}.`,
      rsc: `B. Khan, ChemistryDesk: Adsorption Isotherm Studio, version 1.0.1, Zenodo, ${currentYear}, DOI: ${doi}.`,
      nature: `Khan, B. ChemistryDesk: Adsorption Isotherm Studio. Zenodo https://doi.org/${doi} (${currentYear}).`,
      elsevier: `Khan, B., ${currentYear}. ChemistryDesk: Adsorption Isotherm Studio (Version 1.0.1). Zenodo. https://doi.org/${doi}.`,
      wiley: `B. Khan, ChemistryDesk: Adsorption Isotherm Studio, version 1.0.1, Zenodo, ${currentYear}, DOI: ${doi}.`
    };

    let currentInlineFormat = 'bibtex';

    function updateInlineCite() {
      if (inlineCiteOutput) {
        inlineCiteOutput.textContent = citations[currentInlineFormat] || citations['bibtex'];
      }
    }

    if (toggleCiteBtn && citeDrawer) {
      toggleCiteBtn.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
        e.preventDefault();
        const isHidden = window.getComputedStyle(citeDrawer).display === 'none';
        citeDrawer.style.display = isHidden ? 'block' : 'none';
        toggleCiteBtn.style.background = isHidden ? '#0284c7' : '#e0f2fe';
        toggleCiteBtn.style.color = isHidden ? '#ffffff' : '#0369a1';
        if (isHidden) updateInlineCite();
      });
    }

    inlineTabs.forEach(tab => {
      tab.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
        e.preventDefault();
        inlineTabs.forEach(t => {
          const el = t as HTMLElement;
          el.style.background = '#ffffff';
          el.style.color = '#334155';
          el.style.borderColor = '#cbd5e1';
          el.style.fontWeight = '600';
        });
        const activeTab = tab as HTMLElement;
        activeTab.style.background = '#0f172a';
        activeTab.style.color = '#ffffff';
        activeTab.style.borderColor = '#0f172a';
        activeTab.style.fontWeight = '700';
        currentInlineFormat = activeTab.getAttribute('data-format') || 'bibtex';
        updateInlineCite();
      });
    });

    if (inlineCopyBtn) {
      inlineCopyBtn.addEventListener('click', async (e) => {
        e.preventDefault();
        try {
          await navigator.clipboard.writeText(citations[currentInlineFormat]);
          inlineCopyBtn.textContent = '✅ Copied!';
          setTimeout(() => {
            inlineCopyBtn.textContent = '📋 Copy';
          }, 1800);
        } catch (err) {
          console.error('Failed to copy citation:', err);
        }
      });
    }

    updateInlineCite();

    // Initial Execution
    initializeData();
  </script>

